#include "statistics-declarations.dl"

// Souffle's body aggregate ("?n = count : R(...)") has no FlowLog equivalent:
// FlowLog counts in the rule HEAD, grouping by the head's non-aggregate
// arguments. Every aggregate in this file is therefore guarded, with the Souffle
// rule kept verbatim in the #else so the Souffle build is unchanged.
//
// Two things bite when rewriting one.
//
// FlowLog's count(x) counts DISTINCT VALUES of x, where Souffle counts rows. So
// whatever the Souffle witness left as "_" has to be named and counted as a
// whole tuple -- count((?hctx, ?value)), not count(?value) -- otherwise repeated
// values collapse into one and the count comes out too low.
//
// A head aggregation produces a group only where a witness tuple exists. A rule
// whose guard matches more keys than the witness therefore loses the zero rows
// Souffle would report, and the zero case has to be written out by hand.
//
// Most rules here simply collapse: the guard atom IS the witness, so it is
// dropped and the count moves into the head. Stats_VarCount,
// Stats_InsensValueVarCount, Stats_InsensBaseVarCount, Stats_InsensVarCount,
// Stats_ArrayCount, Stats_InsensValueArrayCount,
// Stats_InsensBaseValueArrayCount, Stats_InsensArrayCount, Stats_FieldCount,
// Stats_InsensValueFieldCount, Stats_InsensBaseValueFieldCount,
// Stats_InsensFieldCount and Stats_MethodContextCount are all of this kind.
//
// Method_NumberOfContexts collapses too, but keeps its guard: the guard binds
// only the group key, and Reachable is derived from ReachableContext, so a
// reachable method always has at least one context and no zero row is lost.
//
// Method_VPTCountPerMethodVariable needs the three-part shape described below,
// for the other reason: its guard Var_DeclaringMethod covers far more vars than
// VarPointsTo does -- on avrora 1.85M of 1.86M declared vars point to nothing --
// so Souffle reports a zero for each of them and FlowLog would drop them all.

// The _StatsSeed relation and fact is needed to work-around a FlowLog limitation.
//
// When a rule counts a whole relation, with nothing else in the body, under
// FlowLog, it needs three parts instead of one, for two separate reasons.
//
// First, the count has to move into the rule head, and a head aggregation
// produces nothing at all when the counted relation is empty -- where Souffle
// still reports 0. Those zero rows are real here: with points-to disabled,
// Stats_ArrayCount is empty and Souffle reports Stats_Arrays(0). So the zero
// case is written out explicitly, as a second rule with a negation.
//
// Second, that zero rule cannot live in the same relation as the aggregate.
// A relation fed by both an aggregate rule and a plain rule makes FlowLog emit
// Rust that does not compile (rustc E0271: the reduce changes the column type,
// and the plain rule's tuple no longer matches). See the KNOWN FLOWLOG DEFECT
// note in macros.dl. So the aggregate gets a private _Agg_<name> relation of its
// own, and <name> is then fed by two ordinary rules.
//
// _StatsSeed exists only to give the zero rule a positive atom; FlowLog rejects
// a rule whose body is nothing but a negation.
//
// Stats_Vars, Stats_InsensVars, Stats_Arrays, Stats_InsensArrays, Stats_Fields,
// Stats_InsensFields, Stats_Methods all fall into this case.


#ifdef FLOWLOG_ENGINE
.decl _StatsSeed(?x:number)
_StatsSeed(0).
#endif // FLOWLOG_ENGINE


